This directory is a derivative of three projects, vendored together because the
released run depends on local modifications to each.

  Vision-DeepResearch   https://github.com/Osilly/Vision-DeepResearch
                        MIT License -- see LICENSE-Vision-DeepResearch
                        Provides the async multi-turn agent workflow that
                        rllm/vision_deepresearch_async_workflow/ is built on.

  rLLM                  https://github.com/agentica-project/rllm
                        Apache License 2.0 -- see rllm/LICENSE
                        Vendored at rllm/rllm/. Provides the agent/workflow
                        trainer, the dataset registry and the reward plumbing.

  verl                  https://github.com/volcengine/verl
                        Apache License 2.0 -- see rllm/verl/LICENSE and
                        rllm/verl/Notice.txt
                        Vendored at rllm/verl/. Provides the PPO/GRPO trainer,
                        the FSDP workers and the vLLM rollout.

What differs from upstream, by area:

  rllm/verl/verl/trainer/ppo/core_algos.py
      The `ema_grpo` advantage estimator: the per-group advantage scale is
      normalized against a per-task exponential moving average, with an
      optional length channel, a warm-start prior and persisted EMA state.

  rllm/verl/verl/workers/{fsdp_workers,actor/dp_actor}.py
      rllm/verl/verl/workers/config/actor.py
      An `override_lr` RPC so a resumed run can be forced onto a new learning
      rate, and vision-tower freezing.

  rllm/verl/verl/trainer/ppo/ray_trainer.py
      rllm/rllm/trainer/verl/agent_workflow_trainer.py
      The learning-rate override call sites, and a guard that stops the run
      when a step would otherwise contribute a zero gradient.

  rllm/vision_deepresearch_async_workflow/
      Tool results may carry images, so a crop or a verification view becomes a
      real multimodal message in the next turn rather than being flattened to
      text. Adds the ten-tool agent (mm_agent/), the per-task reward wiring,
      dynamic response budgets, and the termination/masking rules.

  rllm/rllm/rewards/mm_deepresearch_reward.py
      Task rewards for grounding, spot-the-difference, segmentation (via SAM3)
      and counting.

Only the parts needed to run this training stage are included. Upstream's
documentation, tests, recipes, examples, Docker files and unrelated data
preprocessing are not redistributed here; the dataset registry ships empty.
